00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.867 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Our next guest

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.569 size:78% position:39%
is a "New York Times"
best-selling author.

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:05.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
Her new book,
"Hiding in Plain Sight,"

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:05.905 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
is available now.

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:08.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome back to the sho
Sarah Kendzior.

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:09.142 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How are you, Sarah?

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:11.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
-As well as can be expected.
How are you?

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:14.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm good.
I like that in your bookshel

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:16.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
behind you,
you're using it to very --

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:19.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
very smartly
promote your new book.

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:21.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yes.
Of course.

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:22.389 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Well, we were talking.

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:23.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
You obviously
had a book tour planned.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:26.860
You were actually gonna be
on our show in the studio

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.928 line:92%
back in -- I guess, in March

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:31.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, how has it been
having a book --

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:33.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
a new book out that obviousl
you worked on for years

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:35.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
and not being able to go out
and promote it?

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:38.705
-I mean, I'm sad about it.
I'm sad that I didn't get to

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:40.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, see my readers
face-to-face.

00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:43.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I'm mostly
thinking about safety,

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:45.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I don't want to put anyone
in that position.

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:47.680
And there's certainly people who
are having a much harder tim

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:50.517
in this economy and in thi
public-health crisis than me

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:55.121
The book itself is about the
danger of this administratio

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:57.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the erosion
of stable institutions,

00:00:57.724 --> 00:01:00.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
not just in the present
but over the last 40 years

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:03.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, paradoxically,
this is a good time

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:04.764 line:92%
for the book to come out.

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:06.833
-So, I want to talk about
the book, but real quick,

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:10.136
you recently tweeted the las
time you were on the show,

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:13.873
and, again, it was nice that
you got to see the other guests.

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
-You were backstage.

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:16.910 size:81% position:41% line:92%
You got to meet Ice-T.

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:18.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
And here is the photo
that you tweeted.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
And is it true
that your mother --

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:23.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
Your mother has this framed?
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
I gave it to her
as a Mother's Day gift.

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:26.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I sent it to her,
and she loved it,

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:28.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then, you know,
I surprised her.

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:29.823 line:92%
She has it on her mantel.

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:34.094
Just like every baby boomer,
huge Ice-T fan, "Law &amp; Order."

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:36.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
Completely forgot
that she confiscated

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:38.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
my "Body Count" cassette
in like 1991.

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:40.133 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So, you know...

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:41.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it's a shame because,
you know,

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:43.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
the first guest tonight
was Ice Cube.

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:46.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I like that
there's something thematic

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:48.341 line:92%
about the times on your show

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:50.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
-As long as this doesn't lea
to Vanilla Ice

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:53.713
the third time around, then I'
all good with this trend, so..

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:56.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, last time you were on
you were talking about

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:58.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
your book,
"View from Flyover Country."

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:01.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was a lot about,
sort of --

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:04.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
You had studied
autocratic regimes

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:05.325 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and how they, you know,

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:08.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
have this way
of sneaking up on people.

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:12.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
Exactly what is happening
to the, you know,

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:13.433 size:78% position:39% line:92%
systems they rely on.

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:14.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you obviously
wrote this book,

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:17.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
you couldn't have imagined
the moment we are in right now

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:21.441
but it does sort of predict that
if things don't change,

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:22.408 line:92%
this is the sort of thing

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:24.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
we were gonna end up with,
right?

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:26.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
I mean, I didn't predict

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:27.514 line:92%
that I would be talking to you

00:02:27.514 --> 00:02:30.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
during a plague
from our self-quarantine,

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:35.221 size:88% position:44%
but in terms of malice,
in terms of kleptocracy,

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:39.959
in terms of the profound erosion
of institutional stability

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:42.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
and social trust,
this is what I expected

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:44.030 line:92%
from the Trump administration.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:48.801
Because we've had this kind of
facetious, unearned reliance

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:51.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
on checks and balances
that were never really there

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:54.440
They were not applied at the
start of his administration,

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:58.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he has spent the last
four years annihilating them

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:00.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
purging agencies,
packing courts,

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:03.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, basically
stripping this country dow

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:04.817 line:92%
and selling it for parts.

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:06.386 line:92%
And so, yeah, here we are.

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:07.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You point out that
the media sometimes

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:10.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
will focus
on Trump's ineptitude,

00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:12.258 line:92%
but you think the mistake ther

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:16.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
is it ignores
the more sinister side of it

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:18.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, absolutely.
I think that the media,

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:21.868 size:84% position:42%
as well as many people,
are just comfortable

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:23.002 line:92%
thinking of him as a buffoon

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
that stumbled
into the presidency,

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:27.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
like it was an accident,
but that's not true.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:28.608 line:92%
And as I lay out in the book

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:31.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
he ran or nearly ran
for president five times -

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:34.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
1988, 1996,
he ran in 2000,

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:38.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
he ran in 2012,
he ran in 2016.

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:40.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
And one of
his enduring strategies

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:43.489 size:81% position:41%
has been to cover up
his crime with scandal

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:46.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
and to cover up his malice
with incompetence.

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:50.063
A lot of people are shocke
by his reaction to the pandemic,

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:53.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we haven't had
a national mourning,

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:56.836
that the flag hasn't even
been lowered to commemorat

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:59.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
the victims and the people
who tried to save them.

00:03:59.706 --> 00:04:03.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that's completely in lin
with his character.

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:06.579
You know, when 9/11 happened
his first reaction was to sa

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:08.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
it made his buildings
look taller.

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:10.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
When the 2008
financial collapse happened,

00:04:10.617 --> 00:04:13.920
he said that it was a good thing
for him, that he would profit.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:17.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
And back in 2014,
he went on Fox News and said

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:18.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
that he wanted
economic collapse,

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:22.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he wanted riots
and violence in the street

00:04:22.295 --> 00:04:25.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
because that's what makes
America great again.

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:26.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You don't hold back
in your book

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:28.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
as far as, like, naming names.
-No.

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:30.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I think the way,
a lot of times,

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:33.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
some journalists not only fear
you know,

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:37.043
the shutting down of acces
for projects they may do

00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:40.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the future but also,
you know, for personal safety.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you --
When you are specific

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:45.551
about people, do you ever --
do you ever fear for your safety

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:47.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you write?
-I mean, of course.

00:04:47.687 --> 00:04:49.355 line:92%
Of course I fear for my safety

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:52.692
And we've seen a lot of examples
of this administration

00:04:52.692 --> 00:04:55.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
and people connected to it
threatening people.

00:04:55.395 --> 00:04:57.363 size:81% position:41%
You know, we just had
an impeachment hearing

00:04:57.363 --> 00:04:59.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
where the ambassador to Ukrain
basically said

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:02.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Trump and his goon squa
ordered a hit on her.

00:05:02.902 --> 00:05:03.569 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That's a huge deal,

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:06.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there's a long history
of that kind of action.

00:05:06.606 --> 00:05:08.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, so, yeah,
I worry about my safety.

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:12.478
But I'm more worried that
the truth of this administration

00:05:12.478 --> 00:05:14.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
and its history
isn't being told.

00:05:14.781 --> 00:05:15.815 line:92%
And so that's what, you know

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:19.619
I have chosen to do in this book
and through my other work.

00:05:19.619 --> 00:05:21.421 line:92%
And I don't care about access.

00:05:21.421 --> 00:05:22.322 line:92%
You know, I live in Missouri

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:25.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not worried about not bein
invited to a cocktail part

00:05:25.625 --> 00:05:27.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
or whatever the hell peopl
do in D.C.

00:05:27.527 --> 00:05:30.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so that's never really
been an issue for me.

00:05:30.096 --> 00:05:31.097 line:92%
And then, you know, perversely

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:33.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
it gives me a certain
kind of freedom.

